1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,820
Luke 18. And he told them a parable to the effect that they ought always to pray and not

2
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:15,080
lose heart. He said, In a certain city there was a judge, who neither feared God nor respected man.

3
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:18,800
And there was a widow in that city who kept coming to him and saying,

4
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:26,460
Give me justice against my adversary. For a while he refused, but afterward he said to himself,

5
00:00:26,460 --> 00:00:33,000
Though I neither fear God nor respect man, yet because this widow keeps bothering me,

6
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:38,560
I will give her justice, so that she will not beat me down by her continual coming.

7
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:43,500
And the Lord said, Hear what the unrighteous judge says.

8
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:50,660
And will not God give justice to his elect, who cry to him day and night? Will he delay long over

9
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:55,460
them? I tell you, he will give justice to them speedily. Nevertheless,

10
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:56,440
when the judge says, I will not give justice to him, he will not give justice to him.

11
00:00:56,440 --> 00:01:00,300
When the Son of Man comes, will he find faith on earth?

12
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:04,700
He also told this parable to some who trusted in themselves that they were righteous,

13
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:10,400
and treated others with contempt. Two men went up into the temple to pray,

14
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:17,200
one a Pharisee and the other a tax collector. The Pharisee, standing by himself, prayed thus,

15
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:23,680
God, I thank you that I am not like other men, extortioners, unjust, adulterers,

16
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:26,040
or even like this tax collector.

17
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:31,320
I fast twice a week. I give tithes of all that I get.

18
00:01:32,180 --> 00:01:37,460
But the tax collector, standing far off, would not even lift up his eyes to heaven,

19
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:43,500
but beat his breast, saying, God, be merciful to me, a sinner.

20
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:49,380
I tell you, this man went down to his house justified, rather than the other.

21
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:55,060
For everyone who exalts himself will be humbled, but the one who humbles himself

22
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:56,220
will be exalted.

23
00:01:56,220 --> 00:02:00,740
Now they were bringing even infants to him that he might touch them.

24
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:03,600
And when the disciples saw it, they rebuked them.

25
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:06,220
But Jesus called them to him, saying,

26
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:10,200
Let the children come to me, and do not hinder them.

27
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:13,300
For to such belongs the kingdom of God.

28
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,740
Truly I say to you, whoever does not receive the kingdom of God like a child

29
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:20,380
shall not enter it.

30
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:22,860
And a ruler asked him,

31
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:26,200
Good teacher, what must I do to ensure that I am not a sinner?

32
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:29,500
And Jesus said to him,

33
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:31,620
Why do you call me good?

34
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:33,920
No one is good except God alone.

35
00:02:35,140 --> 00:02:36,120
You know the commandments.

36
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:39,560
Do not commit adultery, do not murder, do not steal,

37
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:43,440
do not bear false witness, honor your father and mother.

38
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:44,940
And he said,

39
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:47,920
All these I have kept from my youth.

40
00:02:48,620 --> 00:02:51,000
When Jesus heard this, he said to him,

41
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:53,540
One thing you still lack.

42
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:56,120
Sell all that you have and distribute,

43
00:02:56,780 --> 00:02:59,100
and you will have treasure in heaven.

44
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:01,500
And come, follow me.

45
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:05,200
But when he heard these things, he became very sad,

46
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:07,480
for he was extremely rich.

47
00:03:08,220 --> 00:03:11,060
Jesus, seeing that he had become sad, said,

48
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:16,140
How difficult it is for those who have wealth to enter the kingdom of God!

49
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:20,200
For it is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle

50
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:23,340
than for a rich person to enter the kingdom of God.

51
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,360
Those who heard it said,

52
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:27,900
Then who can be saved?

53
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:29,420
But he said,

54
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:33,980
What is impossible with men is possible with God.

55
00:03:34,620 --> 00:03:35,700
And Peter said,

56
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:39,420
See, we have left our homes and followed you.

57
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:41,200
And he said to them,

58
00:03:41,940 --> 00:03:43,080
Truly I say to you,

59
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:46,500
there is no one who has left house or wife or brothers

60
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:49,720
or parents or children for the sake of the kingdom of God

61
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:53,040
who will not receive many times more in this time

62
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:55,060
and in the age to come.

63
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:56,520
Eternal life.

64
00:03:57,940 --> 00:04:00,580
And taking the twelve, he said to them,

65
00:04:01,440 --> 00:04:03,760
See, we are going up to Jerusalem,

66
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:07,220
and everything that is written about the Son of Man by the prophets

67
00:04:07,220 --> 00:04:08,160
will be accomplished.

68
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:11,620
For he will be delivered over to the Gentiles

69
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:15,180
and will be mocked and shamefully treated and spit upon.

70
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:18,160
And after flogging him, they will kill him.

71
00:04:18,640 --> 00:04:21,680
And on the third day he will rise.

72
00:04:22,020 --> 00:04:24,380
But they understood none of these things.

73
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:26,740
This saying was hidden from them,

74
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,860
and they did not grasp what was said.

75
00:04:30,340 --> 00:04:32,160
As he drew near to Jericho,

76
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:34,960
a blind man was sitting by the roadside begging.

77
00:04:35,620 --> 00:04:37,300
And hearing a crowd going by,

78
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:39,060
he inquired what this meant.

79
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:40,580
They told him,

80
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:43,300
Jesus of Nazareth is passing by.

81
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,100
And he cried out,

82
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:48,900
Jesus, Son of David,

83
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:51,420
have mercy on me.

84
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:54,000
And those who were in front rebuked him,

85
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:54,360
telling him,

86
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:57,500
But he cried out all the more,

87
00:04:58,260 --> 00:05:02,560
Son of David, have mercy on me.

88
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:06,200
And Jesus stopped and commanded him to be brought to him.

89
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:08,680
And when he came near, he asked him,

90
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:11,360
What do you want me to do for you?

91
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:12,720
He said,

92
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:17,240
Lord, let me recover my sight.

93
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:19,260
And Jesus said to him,

94
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:21,320
Recover your sight.

95
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:23,920
Your faith has made you well.

96
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:26,680
And immediately he recovered his sight

97
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:28,980
and followed him, glorifying God.

98
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:31,680
And all the people, when they saw it,

99
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:33,180
gave praise to God.

100
00:05:33,180 --> 00:05:34,180
Amen.

